      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your suggestion. The reasonfor using sizeof(buf) - 1 in the strncpy() call is to ensure that there is room left for the null-terminator at the end of the string. \n\n- sizeof(buf) gives the total size of the buf array, but it does not account for the null-terminating character (\\0) that needs to be explicitly added at the end of the string to ensure it is properly terminated.\n  \n- Using sizeof(buf) - 1 ensures that we copy only up to the available space in the buffer leaving one byte for the null-terminator which we then manually set by buf[sizeof(buf) - 1] \u003d \\0;\n\nIf we use sizeof(buf) instead there is a risk of overwriting the buffer’s boundary (if buf is not large enough to hold the string plus the null-terminator), leading to potential buffer overflows.\n\nHence, sizeof(buf) - 1 is the safer approach ensuring we don’t overwrite the buffer’s boundary while still protecting against buffer overflow vulnerabilities.",
